      "widgets_values": [
        "4K HAND REPAIR V2 \u2014 ANGELO XTRA-FINE\n\n1. In the large ANGELO node, click Load Image and select the finished 4K image. Keep the original resolution.\n2. The workflow starts in Edit Mode with Fine Upscale, Paint and Area Prompt enabled.\n3. Paint only the malformed fingers and palm, plus the smallest possible amount of wrist. Leave the watch, most of the wrist/forearm and background untouched; the 128 px context setting lets the model see them automatically.\n4. Release the brush to run the repair. Use Re-roll or Vary \u00d74 to try alternatives, then choose/accept the best result.\n5. The Save Image node writes the complete image at its original dimensions.\n\nHAND DEFAULTS\n\u2022 Refine mode; denoise 0.65\n\u2022 Internal repair crop targets 2.0 MP, capped at 6\u00d7. Keeping this above the native hand crop forces Angelo to sample the crop instead of the entire 4K latent.\n\u2022 128 px context, 20 px feather\n\u2022 Reference anchor 0.35 preserves the wrist, lighting and identity\n\u2022 15 steps, CFG 1.2, res_2s + simple (matching the current Klein setup)\n\nFor a smile or another local edit, replace the Area Prompt text inside Angelo and paint only that feature. Use the Remove toggle only when you actually want to delete an object."
      ],
      "title": "START HERE \u2014 hand repair instructions",
      "color": "#243",
      "bgcolor": "#465"
    },
